Error [jet.UnknownField]: `context` has no readable field `scheduler`
  --> tests/ui/context_read_unknown_field.jet:4:19
    |
  4 |     print(context.scheduler)
    |                   ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: The task context reads `allocator` (a `mem.Allocator`), `deadline` (`Int?`, absolute wall milliseconds), `thread` (`Int`, the running thread's index), `logger` (a `log.Handler`), `on_stop` (a `fn(debug.Stop)`), `print` (a `term.PrintStyle`), `scratch` (the task's `mem.Arena`) and `trace` (`[SourceLocation]`, the calling frames)
 Fix: Write `context.allocator`, `context.deadline`, `context.thread`, `context.logger`, `context.on_stop`, `context.print`, `context.scratch` or `context.trace`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0302
